00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.270 align:start position:0%
 
all right let's get into audience  questions for the week david shouldn't  joe biden be bragging about the stock  market the way trump did i don't mean  because joe biden is actually  responsible for the stock market  but because trump seemed to do well when  he bragged about it  i i like the way that this question is  asked because  it's not being asked as a question of  whether joe biden deserves credit i mean  as we've talked about before  to some degree the sort of economic  circumstances uh over which a president  has  some influence impact the stock market  but the stock market performance alone  is often used kind of as a political  football and donald trump  certainly regularly would talk about how  great the stock market is doing when it  was up  not when it was down and many of his  followers fell for it  it's really a question of whether  politically it would be advantageous for  joe biden to do it  i think that it's not clear that it  would because  joe biden's base is so different than  donald trump's base  donald trump's base was  disproportionately made up of people who  were never involved in politics before  or who were and they fell for republican  nonsense  so they were like the perfect marks for  just hearing from trump  about the stock market and the joe biden  base  is different and it doesn't strike me as  something that would  be so obviously beneficial  for joe biden to brag about the stock  market in the same way that donald trump  did now  that being said just because you don't  have  the sort of sycophantic cult of  personality cheerleaders on the left  that you had on the right around donald  trump doesn't mean joe biden shouldn't  talk about the stock market in the  context  of talking about how we're doing so  certainly joe biden should be saying  we're vaccinating more than 3 million a  day  are down 77 percent cases are down  roughly the same percentage  uh unemployment is down we are seeing  job creation  stock market is at record highs on and  up right so it's a package  overall but if the question is should  joe biden  start tweeting about the stock market  from a golf course the way  you know the caricature of what donald  trump was doing i don't think it's  it's what joe biden should be doing one  other aspect to why it's important  for biden to talk about the stock market  numbers  is that you do want to try at least  to get the media to  put out messages that are advantageous  to you  any president would try to do this and  rather than just leaving it to corporate  media to figure out oh the stock market  is doing well and joe biden's president  and we were told that it was going to be  a disaster by trump if joe biden were  president  why not again this this is sort of like  communications in pr  feed the story to the media in in some  sense  one one other aspect of this  when donald trump insisted during the  campaign  that if joe biden wins your 401ks will  be worth nothing  the economy will collapse unemployment  will explode  coveted death will explode suicides will  explode you won't have windows and  buildings you won't have indoor heating  you won't have indoor cooling you'll  have to flush your toilet 10 to 15 times  you'll have to run your dishwasher two  or three times to get your dishes clean  we knew all that stuff was crazy but in  particular now  joe biden talking about what the stock  market is doing  might be a good way to get media outlets  to put more republicans on the spot  and say you agreed with trump during the  campaign that if joe  biden were president this would happen  to the market the markets at record  highs what say you  they would almost certainly retreat to  something like well joe biden has  inflated the stock market by  quote printing money through stimulus  and he wants to do infrastructure  but they'll be on the ropes and they  will have a defense it'll be a really  stupid defense so the  the position joe biden should take is  take  credit for turning things around  and talk about the stock market as one  of many  indicators as to how things are  continuing to improve  what if you could read 10 books in just  one sitting that's exactly what one of  my favorite apps lets you do it's called  blinkist and what they do is take  thousands of popular nonfiction books  they condense them down  into text or audio that you can consume  in 15 minutes  blinkist makes sure that you're getting  all of the  important core insights from each book  so it's perfect for exploring a book you  otherwise wouldn't have time for  if there's a full book you're thinking  about buying you can use blinkist to get  a sample  first just think how much you can enrich  yourself  by being able to soak up an entire  non-fiction book  in just 15 minutes i recently checked  out the book podcast marketing strategy  by daniel rolls and kieran rogers and  so useful so particularly applicable to  what i'm doing  really recommend it blinkist has books  on politics philosophy science they have  27 different non-fiction categories and  a subscription is only about eight bucks  a month  and you get the entire library but  you can try it totally free and get 25  off a subscription  when you go to blinkist.com pacman  i've put the link right underneath this  video

